1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,620
Read a simple A1 laundromat article.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:13,250
Learn what a laundromat is, how people use machines, and how to ask for help before a short role play.

3
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:14,120
Warm-Up Questions.

4
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:19,270
Do you wash clothes at home or outside?

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,520
What clothes do you wash often?

6
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:28,160
What can you ask when a machine is difficult?

7
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:30,140
At the laundromat

8
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,080
Excuse me.

9
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,020
Is this washing machine free?

10
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:34,960
Yes, it is free.

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,340
What do you need to wash?

12
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,400
I need to wash towels.

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,940
This big machine is good for towels.

14
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:42,980
Where do I put detergent?

15
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:44,920
Put it in this small drawer.

16
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,680
Which cycle is normal?

17
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,340
This one is normal.

18
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,220
It takes thirty minutes.

19
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,880
Can I pay by card?

20
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,060
Yes.

21
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,500
Tap your card here.

22
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:55,460
Great.

23
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:56,800
I will come back later.

24
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:58,040
Okay.

25
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:00,160
Please come back in thirty minutes.

26
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:01,960
Final Speaking Task

27
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:03,120
Excuse me.

28
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:05,820
Is this washing machine free?

29
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,520
Yes, it is free.

30
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,800
What do you need to wash?

31
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,740
I need to wash towels.

32
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,360
This big machine is good for towels.

33
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:15,360
Where do I put detergent?

34
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,540
Put it in this small drawer.

35
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:19,180
Which cycle is normal?

36
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:20,620
This one is normal.

37
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,040
It takes thirty minutes.

38
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:27,340
Laundromat English is about clothes, machines, time, and payment.

39
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:32,820
Practice the role play again with one new thing to wash and one new payment method.

40
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:33,540
Good work.

41
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,500
Ask one clear question, repeat the important words, and move when your next step is clear.
